Miss QuoteKnown as "the Suave Siren of Specious Scoops,"she aces stories by smooth-talking witnessesinto silence. However, she constantly jumblesthe facts - without even knowing it, sheremolds the simplest sayings and quotes as ifthey were putty in her hands. Her real "make-upkit" is her notebook, not her compact. But watchout - this femme fatale is one shady lady!Nickname: Queen Bee of the Bogus BylinesMotto: "1,000 words aren't worth an 8"x10" glossy."Last Headline: "Conductor Argues With Orchestra -Fights the Band That Heeds Him"Otto ContextMaster of the one-liner, this guy reports the newslike a stand-up comic. People love his routine,but he never stops moving and never shuts up, soreliable witnesses forget the point after fiveminutes with him. This dangerous dude will twistfacts like pretzels to get a laugh. Marvin namedhim "Cub Reporter With the Most Chutzpah."Nicknames: Motor Mouth; Kid RimshotMotto: "News is like pizza: the cheesier, the better!"Last Headline: "Two-Headed Cow Gives Birth to Its Own Mother While Riding Bicycle on Lake Erie"Leda StrayA field reporter with no sense of direction, sheinsists she grew up in East Dakota. She alsoinsists that the San Francisco earthquake occurred in Tupelo, Mississippi. To her, "Get lost!"is an empty threat. Since she's so often lostherself, she confuses anyone she talks to. Butshe's also incredibly lucky - she always gets toa story fast by not taking the direct route.Nickname: Lucky LedaMotto: "Do you know the way to San Jose?"Last Headline: "Astronauts Land on Mars - On-the-Spot Exclusive"Ruth Liz TacticsShe counts on her frail, elderly appearance toopen doors. But beware - the friendly,grandmotherly type she's not! Ruth knows everytrick and strong-arm tactic in the book. Shesnatches stories away from cub reporters likecandy from a baby. Her editor uses her to teachcommando journalism classes. Her stories havemore arsenic than old lace in them.Nickname: Ma BarkerMotto: "There, there. Tell granny all about it."Last Headline: "Elvis Seen Working as DanceInstructor in Retirement Home"Hood WinkWhen this nickel-and-dime con man went tocollege, he majored - unfortunately - inhypnotism. Now he psychs out witnesses withhis mind-adjustment techniques until they don'tknow which way is up. He also studied zoologyand human psychology - which this cynicalscoopmaster considers almost the same thing.Avoid his clever tongue and penetrating gaze.Nickname: Professor PsychoMotto: "There's power in knowledge - abuse it!"Last Headline: "Man Mistakes His Car for a Hat -Hypnotist Triumphs"Marvin MuckrakerYears after he forged his first note from hismother in second grade, Marvin still misleadswith the pen. He loves slander, half-truths, andinnuendo. He built his paper with his own form ofjournalism - "invent-igation." Since then, he'sruined career after career with his famous"strike while the back is turned" punch. As areporter, he's almost unbeatable. Beware!Nickname: The MucksterMotto: "Sleaze Sells"Last Headline: "Ban Seatbelts and Start Smoking,Doctors Urge"